# Cell from playpick: mode=walk, boss=crowns, spec=druid:restoration,
# style=mash, size=10, difficulty=normal, view=390x844,touch, save=fresh.
#
# "walk" means the long way (example.play's own words): no #hash shortcut to
# the roster, walked in from the front page. The target, crowns (The Three
# Crowns), sits in room `crimson`, past the whole lower spire and across the
# upper crossing -- there is no way to it that skips marrow, whisper, skyward
# and gorged on a fresh save, so this cell is close to the `clear` mode's own
# walk with one difference: it stops once crowns's room is reached rather than
# pushing on. First session to walk this far while aiming at a wing boss by
# name rather than at "as far as it goes".
open
targets
ui
shot front
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:druid:restoration
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot arrive-threshold
state
targets

# Chunk 1: threshold -> vigil -> spire(marrow) -> climb -> oratory(whisper) ->
# mooring(skyward) -> rise(gorged) -> crossing. Generous budget; evening stops
# itself early (evening-stuck) if two rooms in a row go nowhere.
evening mash 90 9
shot after-evening-1
state
says

# Chunk 2: crossing -> crimson wing -> crowns's own room, and the fight.
evening mash 110 4
shot after-evening-2
state
says
bill
targets
ui
